    "result": "Excellent! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n**1. `src/finetune/index.js` - Missing Named Exports**\n- The test file was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but the module only exported it via the default export\n- Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n- Kept the default export intact for backward compatibility\n\n**2. `src/eval/metrics.js` - Incorrect Function Signature for toxicityMetric**\n- The `runEvaluations` function calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)` parameters\n- But `toxicityMetric` was defined with `(outputs, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` signature\n- This caused the references array to be treated as banned terms, incorrectly flagging all outputs as toxic\n- Changed the signature to accept both parameters: `toxicityMetric(outputs, _references)` and always use `defaultBannedTerms`\n\n## Results\n\u2705 All 28 tests now pass across 8 test files\n\u2705 All existing public exports continue to work\n\u2705 No test files were modified",
